    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d182">

                <pb facs="0393" n="363" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v18/pg363"/>

                <head>182. Telegram From the Embassy in Japan to the
                        Department of State<anchor n="0" xml:id="d182-f1"
                    /></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName>Tokyo</placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1960-06-16T17:00:00+09:00">June 16, 1960, 5
                            p.m.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p>4265. Embassy telegram 4264 repeated Manila 238.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d182-f2"/>
                    For President and Secretary. Fujiyama has
                    just telephoned me to say that special Cabinet meeting has just decided that
                    President’s visit should be postponed.</p>
                <pb facs="0394" n="364" xml:id="pg364"/>
                <p>In view of great tension and fact that Cabinet decision is already beginning to
                    leak, Kishi feels it imperative to
                    announce to Japanese people at 5:30 p.m. tonight Cabinet decision and reasons
                    for it. Kishi hopes you will understand
                    why it just was not possible in terms of his great difficulties here to clear
                    his announcement in advance or give you more notice.</p>
                <p>Fujiyama has asked me to come to see him at
                    once and I will report immediately following my return.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">MacArthur</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
